$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a mixture of triflate A1 (2.15 g, 6 mmol), anthracen-9-ylboronic acid
(2.0 g, 9 mmol, 1.5 equiv), potassium fluoride (1.04 g, 18 mmol, 3
equiv), Pd2dba3 (54.9 mg, 0.06 mmol, 1 mol %), BI-DIME (39.6 mg, 0.12
mmol, 2 mo %) was charged degassed dioxane (20 mL). The mixture was
stirred under nitrogen at 100 °C for 24 h, cooled to rt, and then
quenched by addition of water (50 mL) and dichloromethane (50 mL). The
dichloromethane layer was washed sequentially with 10 % NaOH solution (25
mL) and brine (25 mL), dried over sodium sulfate, concentrated, and
purified by column chromatography (eluents: hexane to EtOAc) to provide
the desired coupling product B as a white solid (0.70 g, 1.81 mmol, 30%).
B, yield (0.70 g, 1.81 mmol, 30%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.52 (s, 1H),
8.04 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.99 (m, 1H), 7.76 (m, 1H), 7.66 (t, J = 7.5
Hz, 1H), 7.58 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.40-7.50 (m, 3H), 7.37 (m, 1H), 7.16
(dd, J = 8.4, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (dd, J = 7.4, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 4.47 (m, 2H),
0.45 (d, J = 16.3 Hz, 9H); 31P NMR (162 MHz, CDCl3) δ 62.4; 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.2 (d, J = 18.7 Hz), 141.8 (d, J = 6.3 Hz), 134.6 (d, J
= 1.6 Hz), 134.1 (d, J = 2.0 Hz), 131.3, 131.0, 130.3 (d, J = 2.7 Hz),
128.7, 128.1, 127.8, 127.6, 126.1, 126.0, 125.9, 125.7, 125.4, 124.8,
115.8 (d, J = 88 Hz), 113.6 (d, J = 5.2 Hz), 65.9 (d, J = 60.2 Hz), 33.2
(d, J = 71.5 Hz), 23.6; ESI-MS: m/z 387 [M +H]+.
